### LESSONS LEARNED:

Previous Lessons:
1. Always use '=' followed by a single expression when defining function bodies in Alloy 6; using curly braces for function bodies is only valid for predicates and facts, not functions.
2. Always use curly braces { } for set and relational comprehensions in Alloy; square brackets [ ] are only for function or predicate invocation.
3. Curly-brace set comprehensions cannot be used as function bodies in Alloy 6; functions must return a single expression or quantifier expression of the declared type.**
4. [LESSON]: Always verify that all parentheses and curly braces are balanced and properly nested in Alloy functions and predicates, especially when using nested quantifiers or set comprehensions; missing closures can cause Alloy to report confusing syntax errors at seemingly unrelated locations.
5. Can't use parentheses ( ) for function/predicate application in Alloy 6 → Must use brackets [ ] for arguments.

