Previous Lessons:
1. Syntax errors reported at a function may originate from earlier, incorrectly defined functions; always check for valid function-body syntax in all preceding functions.
2. Always use '=' followed by a single expression when defining function bodies in Alloy 6; using curly braces for function bodies is only valid for predicates and facts, not functions.
3. Always use curly braces { } for set and relational comprehensions in Alloy; square brackets [ ] are only for function or predicate invocation.
4. Curly-brace set comprehensions cannot be used as function bodies in Alloy 6; instead, use '=' followed by a single expression or quantifier expression of the declared type.
