[RATIONALE]:
This fix directly addresses the Alloy 6 rule that function bodies must be a single expression, not a set comprehension in curly braces, and uses a quantified lone-expression instead; this approach is different from previous failed fixes, which only added declarations or braces without correcting the function body format.

[LESSON]:
Always use explicit quantifiers or let-expressions for function bodies in Alloy 6 instead of curly-brace set comprehensions, which are only valid in predicates and facts.
